Cyclo Provider Pooler
---------------------

This package installs a Docker build context at:

    /usr/share/cyclo/components/provider-pooler

It does not start a component, modify /etc/cyclo/host.conf, publish a port, or
store provider credentials. Provider ordering and account-qualified model IDs
are installation-specific, so the operator must add a declaration explicitly.

For example, after configuring the named gateway accounts and confirming their
model IDs with `cyclo models`:

    provider pool /usr/share/cyclo/components/provider-pooler upstream=gateway.provider -- account-a/model account-b/model model=balanced

Place that declaration in the relevant host.conf, then run `cyclo refresh`.
The first image build uses the component's digest-pinned Node base image and
installs the lockfile-pinned production dependencies inside Docker.
